The mathematical formulation linking adult survival under ideal conditions (Sa
) and body mass is detailed in Johnson et al. (2012). This approach is grounded on the Slade et al. (1998)’s assumption that 1% of a new cohort survives to senescence. With α = age at first breeding, ω = age at last breeding (or maximum longevity) and Sj
